Subregion name: stroll_garden
Subregion description: A meticulously landscaped stroll garden with a serpentine koi pond, arched bridge, stone lanterns, and mossy stepping stones.
Subregion plan: A wide, meticulously landscaped stroll garden situated directly behind the main residential pavilion. The central and western portions of the region are occupied by a serpentine koi pond that winds from west to east, featuring organic, stone-lined banks. Crossing the narrowest center section of this pond is a prominent low-arched wooden footbridge that aligns with the pavilion's rear exit steps. A winding walking path of flat, dark slate stepping stones curves through the moss-covered ground, forming a continuous loop that connects the bridge to the eastern and western halves of the garden. On the eastern side, the path weaves around sculpted earth mounds planted with low, cloud-sheared shrubs and dwarf Japanese maples. Along the path's curves and near the water's edge, several weathered gray stone lanterns are positioned next to natural rock arrangements to serve as spatial markers. The entire background is bounded by a dense bamboo grove, while the sides are enclosed by the outer stone-foundation plaster walls.

